cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this Windows port, please cite the upstream Bakta paper (and the
  individual tools you rely on) AND this repository. See the "Citing" section of
  the README for the full list.
title: "Bakta for Windows (native port)"
abstract: >-
  A native-Windows build of Bakta (rapid, standardized bacterial genome
  annotation) together with native-Windows ports of its full tool stack
  (AMRFinderPlus, Infernal, HMMER, tRNAscan-SE, Aragorn, PilerCR) plus bundled
  DIAMOND and BLAST+. Runs without WSL, Docker, Cygwin or a Linux VM.
